% ============================================================================
% phoneme-segmentation.query.adj — a worked recall over the literacy
% phoneme-segmentation library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what sounds does 'feet'
% break into?": it states no linguistics fact — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `phoneme_segmentation` rows and returns the sounds + the
% table's source/locator/trust. The second query runs the relation BACKWARD
% (bind the three sounds `f`, `ee`, `t`, recall the word they segment from).
% A word this source does not demonstrate segmenting is not in the table, so
% a recall on it abstains honestly — the engine never invents a segmentation.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli phoneme-segmentation.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "phoneme-segmentation.adj"

? phoneme_segmentation(feet, $S1, $S2, $S3)   % expect f, ee, t
? phoneme_segmentation($Word, f, ee, t)       % expect feet — reverse recall
? phoneme_segmentation(cat, $S1, $S2, $S3)    % expect abstain — not the word this source demonstrates
